Description: Detects localized periods of decoupling between two time series
    using correlations between local moving averages. Trends are extracted by
    moving average and noise autocovariance is estimated from the residual
    variogram; the local sample correlation is then compared against its value
    under a null of local affine similarity by pointwise one-sided Z-tests.
    Simultaneous inference across overlapping windows uses the step-up
    procedure of Benjamini and Yekutieli (2001)
    <doi:10.1214/aos/1013699998>, controlling the false discovery rate under
    arbitrary dependence. Includes a quality-controlled sample of dissolved
    oxygen and pH monitoring data from the Morro Bay estuary, collected by the
    Central and Northern California Ocean Observing System (CeNCOOS).
